; A dependency's install script runs as you, with your network and your files, before anyone
; reads a line of it. npm only warns about ones it has never been told about; this makes it stop.
; Every install script in the tree is decided in package.json's "allowScripts", all of them denied.
; A dependency upgrade moves past its pinned entry there and fails the install until someone looks
; at what the new version's script does and records that decision.
strict-allow-scripts=true
